  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Office and Station
    
    Light-Regent Lianoshing served Aurora Stack through the Faction Wars as administrative aide and deputy to Light-Regent Xouhoulong (beacon-lit) chang'Rampart, the beacon-keeper turned politician who consolidated power through the Icebound Exchange. Frost-born — marked by the faint silver plumage sheen and crystalline flipper-scarring characteristic of prolonged aurora-magic work — Lianoshing wore the formal white robes of office with silver clasps shaped like closed eyes. Younger penguins attributed this design to what followed his descent into the deep tunnels.
    
    ## Dual Practice
    
    Lianoshing mastered both the Shell Hatch, the aurora-channeled ice-memory reading technique, and Slide Prism, the prismatic harvesting method — the latter learned from Nightshelf adepts. For an Aurora devotee, studying Nightshelf techniques was taboo, though the Flipper Accord nominally required cross-training at the administrative level. The summary record states plainly that Lianoshing never quite forgave himself for it. Xouhoulong, by contrast, trusted him absolutely. The asymmetry is instructive.
    
    ## The Hearth Plaza and the Sealed Chambers
    
    Lianoshing carried Xouhoulong's schematics for the Hearth Plaza for two years, recalibrating refraction angles when the crystal-cutters failed them. He knew the plaza's geometry better than anyone except its designer — including the sealed research chambers beneath the lowest level. Those chambers housed experiments into deep-ice pressure-magic that ended with two researchers lost to something the ice answered. The chronicle account from "Light and Ruin" confirms these galleries later became corruption corridors that undermined the structure Xouhoulong built.
    
    ## The Ledgers
    
    Lianoshing's administrative precision was legendary and, ultimately, a tool of deception. He died in the Frozen Peace era, still maintaining his ledgers. Afterward, the colony discovered he had padded fire-core allocation numbers for three seasons, diverting small quantities to heat the lower caverns where surface penguins too weak for crystal-spire labor had been quietly freezing to death. No formal inquiry followed. The memorial stones record no theft.
    
    He was also custodian of the Crystalline Lineage, the aurora-inscribed genealogical tome of Aurora Stack's founding families.
    
    ## Oral Tradition (Contested)
    
    Fable tradition assigns Lianoshing two additional roles unsupported by ice-memory: mediator during the Thron∴mbra Fracta — the succession crisis that fractured the Nightshelf into three warring factions — where all three claimants refused him; and prophet of the Collapse, the catastrophic ice-fracture of the Promenade Ward, where he warned Aurora Stack elders three times and was ignored. His dual mastery gave him the knowledge to predict the disaster but not, apparently, the authority to prevent it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
